//@version=6
indicator("RIOT 8003 L UNIFIED (STD + Counter)", overlay=true, max_boxes_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500)

// ============================================================================
// MERGE NOTES:
// - Combines the STD-PLAIN primary order-flow entry system with the Counter
//   (fade) entry system into ONE script/state machine, sharing one impulse
//   engine instead of two separate copies.
// - OB and REV order-flow types are DROPPED. Only STD order flows exist.
// - Counter arming is a CONTINUOUS check on every confirmed bar while the
//   STD trade is open (not a one-shot "first bar only" check) â€” this matches
//   the methodology actually used in the historical $-P&L backtest, so the
//   validated results (win rate, speed, net $ at 10m/15m/30m/2h) apply.
// - ANYTHING THAT CONFIRMS GOES STRAIGHT TO THE EXCHANGE. Nothing is held
//   inside the indicator waiting to be triggered. The STD fires its alert at
//   confirmation; the Counter fires its alert the moment it ARMS. Both then
//   rest as real orders on Bybit and the exchange fills them at the exact
//   level. Pine only mirrors what should be happening.
// - Dynamic SL: the STD order flow has NO stop-loss until its Counter actually
//   opens. The counter's arm alert carries a "close_original" block, but the
//   bot must apply it ONLY on the counter's ENTRY FILL event â€” never on alert
//   receipt â€” and as a PARTIAL POSITION stop, not a reduce-only limit. Both
//   requirements are explained above build_counter_arm_payload(); getting
//   either wrong breaks the mechanism. Requires bot support for
//   "close_original" and "cancel_close_original".
// - If Counter Trade is disabled and the STD box's far end still gets swept,
//   the STD flow is simply marked closed with no SL price (matches the
//   "only if counter is activated" rule literally).
// - Whether a CLOSED STD order flow is kept for review or dropped from tracking
//   is a user toggle (History / Retention). Whenever a record is dropped, its
//   drawn objects are deleted first so nothing is orphaned on the chart.
// - Long and short entries carry separate margin inputs on both the STD leg
//   and the Counter leg, matching the live bot's asymmetric long/short cost
//   structure. The counter's inputs are named by the ORDER FLOW they hedge,
//   not by the counter's own direction â€” see the note at the inputs.
// - TP is re-checked every bar even after a counter has armed/filled. If price
//   recovers to the STD's own TP while a counter is live, the STD closes on its
//   own TP and a "cancel_close_original" alert fires to pull the now-orphaned
//   SL off that position.
// - A COUNTER IS NEVER KILLED BY WHAT THE ORIGINAL DOES. Once armed it runs its
//   own lifecycle â€” armed -> filled -> its own TP â€” because its entry limit is
//   a real live order on Bybit. Marking it finished when the original closes
//   would desync Pine from that order and would also count a counter that never
//   opened as "Done".
//   Its state machine therefore lives in its OWN loop (section 9b), NOT nested
//   inside the order flow loop. Nesting it was a real bug: the instant the
//   original closed and left of_watch, the only code advancing its counter went
//   with it and the counter froze in ACTIVE forever â€” live charts had 129 of
//   357 counters stuck that way, boxes stretched to the right edge, ignoring
//   every TP the price crossed.
// - âš  A COUNTER IS ONLY SENT IF ITS ORIGINAL WAS SENT. Pine rebuilds this whole
//   state machine from history whenever the script loads or an input changes,
//   and historical bars fire NO alerts. A flow that never reached its TP stays
//   ACTIVE and is the last thing the trim evicts, so a replayed flow can live
//   for months and then have its far end swept on a REALTIME bar â€” firing an
//   arm alert for an id the bot has never seen. The bot then opens the counter,
//   cannot resolve the original, and leaves it running with no hedge and no
//   stop. That happened live on 8003 on 2026-08-19: a counter armed from a
//   2026-05-22 order flow. Each flow now records whether its own entry alert
//   really went out (live_entry) and the counter inherits it (bot_linked).
//   Unlinked counters are still tracked and drawn â€” greyed out and marked
//   CHART ONLY, counted separately in the table â€” but nothing is ever sent.
// - The counter's OWN TP is only evaluated on bars AFTER its fill bar, and it
//   is bookkeeping only (no alert) â€” the real closes are already resting on the
//   exchange. The guard still matters so the chart/table don't mark a counter
//   completed on the very bar it filled.
// - Counter box visualization also draws the ORIGINAL signal's entry/TP as
//   dashed reference lines, so once the original's own box is deleted (on
//   close) its levels are still visible next to the counter that replaced it.
//
// VISUALS:
// - Scale anchor plot so the price scale never collapses when drawings are off.
// - Optional STD info label (off by default) on FILLED flows only: state,
//   entry, TP + distance %, SL once live, and the id used in the alerts.
// - Live markers: on the last bar, a compact price tag past the current candle
//   for every live level (STD entry/TP/SL and Counter entry/TP).
// - History is user-controlled per side (History / Retention group): KEEP
//   decides whether a completed record survives at all, SHOW decides whether
//   its drawings are on the chart. NOTE: "Keep completed STD order flows" is
//   OFF by default â€” with it off a closed flow's box is deleted, so the "show
//   completed" toggle beneath it has nothing left to display. Turn KEEP on
//   first if you want closed STD zones to stay visible.
//
// CAPACITY â€” MAX_WATCH / MAX_CTR are a TRIM TARGET ONLY, never a gate on
// signal creation. An order flow is always created and always alerts; the trim
// only decides what ages out. This matters: an earlier version gated creation
// on array size, so once the array filled the indicator silently stopped
// producing order flows AND stopped firing alerts to the bot â€” a mute failure
// with no error anywhere. Eviction order is CLOSED first, then PENDING (a
// resting entry that never filled has no path to close itself, so stale ones
// would clog the array forever â€” these are what actually pile up), and only
// then anything else, so a live ACTIVE/ARMED position is the last thing
// dropped.
// ============================================================================

// ============================== 1. INPUTS ==============================
gT = "Trade"
in_std_enable     = input.bool(true, "Enable STD Order Flow", group=gT, tooltip="Controls whether STD entries actually fire the primary alert. Structure tracking (needed for Counter) always runs regardless.")
in_counter_enable = input.bool(true, "Enable Counter Trade", group=gT, tooltip="Controls whether a Counter (fade) position is ever armed/traded when a STD order flow's far end is swept.")
in_roi     = input.float(25.0, "Target ROI %", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group=gT)
in_lev     = input.float(50.0, "Leverage", minval=1.0, step=1.0, group=gT)
in_std_long_margin  = input.float(1.00, "STD Order Flow Margin â€” Long (USDT)",  step=0.01, group=gT)
in_std_short_margin = input.float(0.33, "STD Order Flow Margin â€” Short (USDT)", step=0.01, group=gT)
// Counter margins are named by the ORDER FLOW they hedge, not by the counter's
// own direction â€” a counter is always the opposite side of its original, so
// naming them by their own direction inverts the pairing and silently breaks
// the size ratio. "for LONG order flows" is a SHORT counter, and vice versa.
in_ctr_for_long_margin  = input.float(4.00, "Counter Margin â€” for LONG order flows (USDT)",  step=0.01, group=gT, tooltip="Margin of the counter that hedges a LONG order flow. That counter is itself a SHORT. Keep this at the intended multiple of 'STD Order Flow Margin â€” Long'.")
in_ctr_for_short_margin = input.float(1.32, "Counter Margin â€” for SHORT order flows (USDT)", step=0.01, group=gT, tooltip="Margin of the counter that hedges a SHORT order flow. That counter is itself a LONG. Keep this at the intended multiple of 'STD Order Flow Margin â€” Short'.")

gM = "Rule Mode"
in_mode  = input.string("STD-plain", "Rule mode", options=["STD-plain","STD-ORBK"], group=gM, tooltip="STD-plain = unfiltered STD (recommended: ~9x more signals, same ~99% close quality). STD-ORBK = legacy filtered behavior. The ORBK flag is still recorded/tagged in the alert either way.")
in_debug = input.bool(false, "Debug: mark ALL STD (grey)", group=gM)

gB = "Bot"
// syminfo.ticker auto-resolves to the chart's symbol (e.g. TAOUSDT.P) — no manual input needed.
in_inst = syminfo.ticker

gD = "Direction"
in_dir = input.string("Bullish", "Direction", options=["Bullish","Bearish"], group=gD, tooltip="Run one Bullish copy + one Bearish copy.")

gV = "Visual"
in_show_box       = input.bool(true, "Show STD box", group=gV)
in_show_mk        = input.bool(true, "Show STD markers", group=gV)
in_show_tp        = input.bool(true, "Show STD entry/TP/SL lines", group=gV)
in_show_counter        = input.bool(true, "Show Counter boxes", group=gV)
in_show_ctr_orig_lines = input.bool(false, "  â”” Also draw the original's entry/TP on Counter boxes", group=gV, tooltip="Adds 2 dashed reference lines per counter showing the levels of the order flow it hedges. OFF by default: it doubles the counter's line cost from 2 to 4 and the chart runs out of the 500-line budget, after which Pine silently deletes the oldest lines. If you turn this on, lower MAX_CTR in the code to about 50.")
in_show_ctr_unlinked   = input.bool(true, "  â”” Show chart-only Counters (not sent to bot)", group=gV, tooltip="Counters armed from an order flow that Pine rebuilt during history replay. No order for them exists on the exchange â€” they are drawn greyed out and marked CHART ONLY. Turn off to see only counters that were really sent.")
in_show_std_lbl   = input.bool(false, "Show STD info labels (filled only)", group=gV, tooltip="Text label on each FILLED STD order flow showing entry / TP / SL / id. Off by default because a busy chart can carry many open flows at once.")
in_show_live      = input.bool(true, "Show live markers at right edge", group=gV, tooltip="On the last bar, print the price of every live position (STD and Counter) at the current bar so the numbers are readable without hovering.")
in_show_table     = input.bool(true, "Show stats table", group=gV)
in_tbl_pos        = input.string("Top Right", "Table position",
     options=["Top Right","Top Left","Top Center","Middle Right","Middle Left",
              "Middle Center","Bottom Right","Bottom Left","Bottom Center"], group=gV)

// Retention is deliberately separate from visibility: KEEP decides whether the
// record survives at all (memory + stats), SHOW only decides whether its
// drawings are on the chart. That way history can be retained while the chart
// stays clean, or cleared entirely when it isn't wanted.
gH = "History / Retention"
in_keep_std_done  = input.bool(false, "Keep completed STD order flows",   group=gH, tooltip="OFF: a closed STD flow is dropped from tracking and its drawings deleted (lowest memory, no history). ON: the record is kept so its zone can stay on the chart for review. Closed records are always evicted before open ones when the tracking array fills, so keeping history never pushes a live position out of tracking.")
in_show_std_done  = input.bool(true,  "  â”” Show completed STD on chart",  group=gH, tooltip="Only applies when 'Keep completed STD order flows' is ON. Turn off to keep the records but hide the drawings.")
in_keep_ctr_done  = input.bool(true,  "Keep completed Counter trades",    group=gH, tooltip="OFF: a finished counter is dropped from tracking and its drawings deleted. ON: kept for review.")
in_show_counter_done = input.bool(true, "  â”” Show completed Counter on chart", group=gH, tooltip="Only applies when 'Keep completed Counter trades' is ON.")

bool IS_BULL = in_dir == "Bullish"
bool GATED   = in_mode == "STD-ORBK"
string tf_actual = timeframe.period
[tf_open, tf_high, tf_low, tf_close, tf_time] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf_actual, [open, high, low, close, time], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)

// Scale anchor â€” an invisible plot keeps the price scale tied to price even
// when every other drawing is off-screen or hidden, so the chart never
// auto-scales to nothing.
plot(close, title="Scale Anchor", color=color.new(color.white, 100), editable=false)

// ============================== 2. HELPERS ==============================
get_table_pos(s) =>
    switch s
        "Top Right"     => position.top_right
        "Top Left"      => position.top_left
        "Top Center"    => position.top_center
        "Middle Right"  => position.middle_right
        "Middle Left"   => position.middle_left
        "Middle Center" => position.middle_center
        "Bottom Right"  => position.bottom_right
        "Bottom Left"   => position.bottom_left
        "Bottom Center" => position.bottom_center
        =>                 position.top_right

f_det_id(t, is_long) =>
    str.tostring(t) + (is_long ? "L" : "S")

// "price" is ALWAYS sent, on market orders too. The bot derives the take-profit
// from it (`tp_base = price if price is not None else trigger_price`), and the
// TP must be anchored to the ORDER FLOW'S LEVEL â€” never to the confirmation
// candle's close. Omitting it on the deep/market path made the bot anchor the
// TP to the close, so Bybit ended up holding a TP at a different price than the
// one Pine drew and tracked. On market orders Bybit ignores `price` (only LIMIT
// forwards it), so sending it always is safe and only fixes the TP anchor.
build_payload(is_long, entry, tp, cur, margin, rule, ofid) =>
    string act = is_long ? "enter_long" : "enter_short"
    float cost = margin * in_lev
    bool deep = is_long ? (cur <= entry) : (cur >= entry)
    string otype = deep ? "market" : "limit"
    '{"id": "' + ofid + '", "interval": "' + tf_actual + '", "trigger_price": "' + str.tostring(cur) + '", "tv_instrument": "' + in_inst + '", "action": "' + act + '", "order": {"price": "' + str.tostring(entry, "#.#####") + '", "amount": "' + str.tostring(cost) + '", "currency_type": "quote", "order_type": "' + otype + '"}, "take_profit": {"enabled": true, "steps": [{"order_type": "limit", "price_percent": ' + str.tostring(is_long ? (in_roi / in_lev) : -(in_roi / in_lev), "#.####") + ', "volume_percent": 100}]}, "rule_type": "' + rule + '"}'

// Counter ARM payload â€” fired the moment the counter is confirmed (the far end
// swept), at that candle's close. Anything that confirms goes straight to the
// exchange: the counter's entry limit rests on Bybit from here and Bybit fills
// it at the exact level. Pine does NOT wait to detect the touch itself â€” doing
// so was late by up to a full bar, missed wick fills, and could downgrade the
// entry to a market order.
//
// It carries "close_original", the dynamic SL for the ORIGINAL, with two hard
// requirements on the receiving bot:
//
// âš  "place_on": "entry_fill" â€” the SL is set ONLY at the instant the counter's
//   entry actually fills, together with the counter's own TP, and NEVER on
//   receipt of this alert. The entry can rest unfilled (price wicks the level
//   and rejects); setting the SL early would leave the original stopped with no
//   counter to offset it. Pairing must be absolute: counter open <=> SL set.
//
// âš  "mode": "partial_position_sl" â€” it must be a PARTIAL position stop, not a
//   reduce-only limit and not a full-position stop.
//   â€¢ Not a limit: an SL sits on the ACTIVE side of the book, so a sell-limit
//     below market (long) or buy-limit above market (short) is immediately
//     marketable and fills the instant it is placed â€” closing the original at
//     the counter's ENTRY instead of waiting for the trigger.
//   â€¢ Not full-position: on Bybit every same-side flow merges into ONE
//     aggregated position, so a full-position stop would fire the entire book
//     on a single flow's level.
//   Size comes from the original's own fill, which the bot has stored under
//   this same id.
build_counter_arm_payload(is_long, entry, cur, margin, ofid, sl_trigger) =>
    string act  = is_long ? "enter_long" : "enter_short"
    float  cost = margin * in_lev
    bool   deep = is_long ? (cur <= entry) : (cur >= entry)
    string otype = deep ? "market" : "limit"
    '{"id": "' + ofid + '", "interval": "' + tf_actual + '", "trigger_price": "' + str.tostring(cur) + '", "tv_instrument": "' + in_inst + '", "action": "' + act + '", "order": {"price": "' + str.tostring(entry, "#.#####") + '", "amount": "' + str.tostring(cost) + '", "currency_type": "quote", "order_type": "' + otype + '"}, "take_profit": {"enabled": true, "steps": [{"order_type": "limit", "price_percent": ' + str.tostring(is_long ? (in_roi / in_lev) : -(in_roi / in_lev), "#.####") + ', "volume_percent": 100}]}, "rule_type": "COUNTER", "close_original": {"id": "' + ofid + '", "mode": "partial_position_sl", "trigger_price": "' + str.tostring(sl_trigger, "#.#####") + '", "order_type": "market", "place_on": "entry_fill", "reason": "STD_DYNAMIC_SL"}}'

// Pull the now-orphaned SL off the ORIGINAL when it closes on its OWN take
// profit. Only meaningful once the counter has actually filled, because that is
// when the SL was set. NOTE: if Bybit turns out to auto-remove a partial SL when
// the position closes, this alert becomes redundant â€” pending verification.
build_cancel_sl_payload(ofid, cur) =>
    '{"id": "' + ofid + '", "tv_instrument": "' + in_inst + '", "action": "cancel_close_original", "reason": "STD_TP_HIT_FIRST", "trigger_price": "' + str.tostring(cur) + '"}'

tp_of(is_long, e) => is_long ? e * (1 + (in_roi / 100) / in_lev) : e * (1 - (in_roi / 100) / in_lev)

// ============================== 3. TYPES ==============================
type OrderFlow
    bool   is_bull
    bool   is_orbk
    float  box_top
    float  box_bot
    float  entry_price
    float  tp_price
    float  sl_price
    int    conf_bar
    int    conf_time
    bool   entered
    bool   tp_hit
    bool   armed
    bool   sl_hit
    float  counter_entry
    float  counter_tp
    string state          // PENDING, ACTIVE, ARMED, CLOSED
    int    fill_bar
    // TRUE only if this flow's entry alert actually went out to the bot, i.e.
    // it was confirmed on a REALTIME bar with STD alerts enabled. Flows rebuilt
    // during Pine's history replay have this FALSE â€” the bot has never heard of
    // them, so nothing that references their id may be sent to the exchange.
    bool   live_entry
    box    b_ref
    line   en_ref
    line   tp_ref
    line   sl_ref
    label  lbl_ref
    string id

type CounterRecord
    bool   is_long
    float  entry_price
    float  tp_price
    float  box_top
    float  box_bot
    int    entry_time
    int    conf_time
    int    conf_bar
    string state          // ARMED, ACTIVE, INACTIVE
    int    end_time
    int    fill_bar
    // TRUE when the arm alert was actually sent, i.e. the ORIGINAL was itself
    // alerted live so the bot can resolve the id. FALSE = chart-only record:
    // it is drawn and counted for study, but no order of any kind exists for
    // it on the exchange and no alert will ever fire from it.
    bool   bot_linked
    box    b_ref
    line   en_ref
    line   tp_ref
    line   orig_en_ref
    line   orig_tp_ref
    label  lbl_ref
    string of_id

// ============================== 4. STATE ==============================
var float last_valid_high = na
var float last_valid_low  = na
var bool  root_init = false
var int   lbv_bar = na
var int   lgv_bar = na
var float lbv_high = na
var float lbv_low  = na
var float lgv_high = na
var float lgv_low  = na
var bool  in_UI = false
var bool  in_LI = false
var int   ui_id = 0
var int   li_id = 0
var int   ui_start = na
var int   li_start = na
var float ui_hh = na
var float ui_ll = na
var float ui_pl = na
var float li_hh = na
var float li_ll = na
var float li_ph = na
var bool  ui_done = false
var bool  li_done = false
var bool  ui_ended_ob = false
var bool  li_ended_ob = false
var float c_ui_hh = na
var float c_ui_ll = na
var int   c_ui_start = na
var float c_li_hh = na
var float c_li_ll = na
var int   c_li_start = na
var float pB_lvl = na
var float pB_boxlow = na
var int   pB_boxbar = na
var float pS_lvl = na
var float pS_boxhigh = na
var int   pS_boxbar = na
var int   pB_uiid = na
var int   pS_liid = na
// ---- ORBK FVG trackers (informational tag only, both modes) ----
var float uf_Chigh = na
var float uf_top = na
var float uf_bot = na
var int   uf_vc = na
var int   uf_form_bar = na
var bool  uf_ready = false
var bool  uf_exists = false
var bool  uf_mitig = false
var float li_Clow = na
var float lf_top = na
var float lf_bot = na
var int   lf_vc = na
var int   lf_form_bar = na
var bool  lf_ready = false
var bool  lf_exists = false
var bool  lf_mitig = false

// ---- unified order-flow / counter tracking ----
var array<OrderFlow>     of_watch = array.new<OrderFlow>()
var array<CounterRecord> counters = array.new<CounterRecord>()
// Tracking capacity. This is ONLY a trim target for the arrays â€” it never
// gates signal creation. Order flows and counters are always created and
// always alert; the trim below decides what ages out when capacity is reached.
//
// The caps are sized by the LINE budget, which is the binding constraint â€”
// `max_lines_count` is 500 and Pine silently deletes the oldest line once that
// is exceeded, leaving old boxes stripped of their levels with no error.
//   STD flow  : 3 lines (entry, TP, SL)  -> 100 x 3 = 300
//   Counter   : 2 lines (entry, TP)      ->  80 x 2 = 160   [4 if the original
//               reference lines are switched on â€” see in_show_ctr_orig_lines]
//   worst case                              = 460  < 500  OK
// Turning the counter's original-reference lines ON raises the counter cost to
// 320 and the worst case to 620, which OVERFLOWS. That input is off by default
// for exactly this reason; if it is turned on, drop MAX_CTR to ~50.
var int MAX_WATCH = 100
var int MAX_CTR   = 80

// ---- persistent stats (survive array trims/removals) ----
var int std_total         = 0
var int std_completed     = 0
var int counter_total     = 0
var int counter_completed = 0
var int n_gate_pass = 0
var int n_gate_fail = 0

var table stat_tbl = na

if not root_init and bar_index == 0
    last_valid_high := tf_high
    last_valid_low  := tf_low
    root_init := true

ui_done := false
li_done := false
ui_ended_ob := false
li_ended_ob := false

// ============================== 5. VALIDITY ==============================
bool bull_v  = tf_high >= last_valid_high
bool bear_v  = tf_low  <= last_valid_low
bool neutral = not bull_v and not bear_v
bool ob = false
if bar_index > 0 and not na(last_valid_high) and not na(last_valid_low)
    ob := (tf_high >= last_valid_high) and (tf_low <= last_valid_low)

// ============================== 6. IMPULSE MANAGEMENT ==============================
if ob
    if in_UI
        c_ui_ll := ui_ll
        c_ui_hh := ui_hh
        c_ui_start := ui_start
        ui_done := true
        ui_ended_ob := true
        ui_id += 1
        in_UI := true
        ui_start := bar_index
        ui_hh := tf_high
        ui_ll := tf_low
        ui_pl := tf_low
        uf_Chigh := tf_high
        uf_vc := 0
        uf_ready := false
        uf_exists := false
        uf_mitig := false
    if in_LI
        c_li_hh := li_hh
        c_li_ll := li_ll
        c_li_start := li_start
        li_done := true
        li_ended_ob := true
        li_id += 1
        in_LI := true
        li_start := bar_index
        li_hh := tf_high
        li_ll := tf_low
        li_ph := tf_high
        li_Clow := tf_low
        lf_vc := 0
        lf_ready := false
        lf_exists := false
        lf_mitig := false

if in_UI and bear_v and not na(ui_pl) and not ob
    if tf_low <= ui_pl
        c_ui_ll := ui_ll
        c_ui_hh := ui_hh
        c_ui_start := ui_start
        ui_done := true
        ui_ended_ob := false
        in_UI := false
        ui_start := na

if bull_v and not ob
    if not in_UI
        ui_id += 1
        in_UI := true
        ui_start := na(lbv_bar) ? bar_index : lbv_bar
        ui_hh := tf_high
        ui_ll := na(lbv_low) ? tf_low : lbv_low
        ui_pl := tf_low
        uf_Chigh := na(lbv_high) ? tf_high : lbv_high
        uf_vc := 0
        uf_ready := false
        uf_exists := false
        uf_mitig := false
    else
        ui_hh := math.max(ui_hh, tf_high)
        ui_ll := math.min(ui_ll, tf_low)
        ui_pl := math.max(ui_pl, tf_low)
if in_UI and neutral
    ui_ll := math.min(ui_ll, tf_low)

if in_LI and bull_v and not na(li_ph) and not ob
    if tf_high >= li_ph
        c_li_hh := li_hh
        c_li_ll := li_ll
        c_li_start := li_start
        li_done := true
        li_ended_ob := false
        in_LI := false
        li_start := na

if bear_v and not ob
    if not in_LI
        li_id += 1
        in_LI := true
        li_start := na(lgv_bar) ? bar_index : lgv_bar
        li_hh := na(lgv_high) ? tf_high : lgv_high
        li_ll := tf_low
        li_ph := tf_high
        li_Clow := na(lgv_low) ? tf_low : lgv_low
        lf_vc := 0
        lf_ready := false
        lf_exists := false
        lf_mitig := false
    else
        li_ll := math.min(li_ll, tf_low)
        li_hh := math.max(li_hh, tf_high)
        li_ph := math.min(li_ph, tf_high)
if in_LI and neutral
    li_hh := math.max(li_hh, tf_high)

// ============================== 7. ORBK FVG (tag only) ==============================
if not neutral and not ob
    if in_UI and not uf_ready and not na(uf_vc)
        uf_vc += 1
        if uf_vc == 2
            uf_ready := true
            if uf_Chigh < tf_low
                uf_exists := true
                uf_bot := uf_Chigh
                uf_top := tf_low
                uf_form_bar := bar_index
    if in_LI and not lf_ready and not na(lf_vc)
        lf_vc += 1
        if lf_vc == 2
            lf_ready := true
            if li_Clow > tf_high
                lf_exists := true
                lf_bot := tf_high
                lf_top := li_Clow
                lf_form_bar := bar_index

if uf_exists and not uf_mitig and not na(uf_form_bar) and bar_index > uf_form_bar and tf_low <= uf_top
    uf_mitig := true
if lf_exists and not lf_mitig and not na(lf_form_bar) and bar_index > lf_form_bar and tf_high >= lf_bot
    lf_mitig := true

// ============================== 8. STD CONFIRM -> CREATE ORDER FLOW ==============================
if barstate.isconfirmed
    if li_done and not na(c_li_hh) and in_UI
        pB_lvl := c_li_hh
        pB_boxlow := c_li_ll
        pB_boxbar := c_li_start
        pB_uiid := ui_id
    if ui_done and not na(c_ui_ll) and in_LI
        pS_lvl := c_ui_ll
        pS_boxhigh := c_ui_hh
        pS_boxbar := c_ui_start
        pS_liid := li_id

    // ---- Bullish STD candidate ----
    // VALIDITY RULE: an INVALID (neutral / inside) candle can never CONFIRM an
    // order flow. Confirmation is a structural event, so it requires a candle
    // that actually moved structure. A neutral candle touching the level is
    // ignored entirely â€” it neither confirms nor invalidates, so the pending
    // level stays armed for a later valid candle.
    // Execution is NOT gated by this: any candle, valid or not, can fill an
    // entry, hit a take profit, or trigger a stop.
    if not na(pB_lvl)
        if (not in_UI) or (ui_id != pB_uiid)
            pB_lvl := na
            pB_uiid := na
        else if not neutral and tf_high >= pB_lvl
            if math.max(tf_open, tf_close) >= pB_lvl
                bool orbk    = uf_exists and not uf_mitig and not li_ended_ob
                bool gate_ok = GATED ? orbk : true
                string rtag  = orbk ? "STD_ORBK" : "STD"
                if in_debug and IS_BULL
                    label.new(bar_index, tf_low, "s", yloc=yloc.belowbar, style=label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.gray, 50), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
                if IS_BULL and gate_ok
                    n_gate_pass := n_gate_pass + (orbk ? 1 : 0)
                    n_gate_fail := n_gate_fail + (orbk ? 0 : 1)
                    float tp = tp_of(true, pB_lvl)
                    string ofid = f_det_id(tf_time, true)
                    std_total += 1
                    // alert() is a no-op on historical bars â€” only a REALTIME
                    // confirmation actually reaches the bot. Record which one
                    // this was: it decides whether anything referencing this
                    // flow's id may later be sent to the exchange.
                    bool sent_live = barstate.isrealtime and in_std_enable
                    if in_std_enable
                        alert(build_payload(true, pB_lvl, tp, tf_close, in_std_long_margin, rtag, ofid), alert.freq_all)
                    box  bref = na
                    if in_show_box and not na(pB_boxbar)
                        bref := box.new(pB_boxbar, pB_lvl, bar_index, pB_boxlow, border_color=color.new(orbk ? color.teal : #26a69a, 0), border_width=2, bgcolor=color.new(orbk ? color.teal : #26a69a, 80))
                    if in_show_mk
                        label.new(bar_index, tf_low, orbk ? "V" : "v", yloc=yloc.belowbar, style=label.style_label_up, color=color.new(orbk ? color.teal : #26a69a, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
                    line enref = na
                    line tpref = na
                    if in_show_tp
                        enref := line.new(bar_index, pB_lvl, bar_index, pB_lvl, color=color.new(#26a69a, 0), width=2)
                        tpref := line.new(bar_index, tp, bar_index, tp, color=color.new(#26a69a, 40), width=1, style=line.style_dashed)
                        label.new(bar_index, tp, "TP " + str.tostring(tp, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(orbk ? color.teal : #26a69a, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
                    array.push(of_watch, OrderFlow.new(is_bull=true, is_orbk=orbk, box_top=pB_lvl, box_bot=pB_boxlow, entry_price=pB_lvl, tp_price=tp, sl_price=na, conf_bar=bar_index, conf_time=tf_time, entered=false, tp_hit=false, armed=false, sl_hit=false, counter_entry=pB_boxlow, counter_tp=tp_of(false, pB_boxlow), state="PENDING", fill_bar=na, live_entry=sent_live, b_ref=bref, en_ref=enref, tp_ref=tpref, sl_ref=na, lbl_ref=na, id=ofid))
            pB_lvl := na

    // ---- Bearish STD candidate ----
    // Same validity rule as the bullish side: no confirmation on a neutral bar.
    if not na(pS_lvl)
        if (not in_LI) or (li_id != pS_liid)
            pS_lvl := na
            pS_liid := na
        else if not neutral and tf_low <= pS_lvl
            if math.min(tf_open, tf_close) <= pS_lvl
                bool orbk    = lf_exists and not lf_mitig and not ui_ended_ob
                bool gate_ok = GATED ? orbk : true
                string rtag  = orbk ? "STD_ORBK" : "STD"
                if in_debug and not IS_BULL
                    label.new(bar_index, tf_high, "s", yloc=yloc.abovebar, style=label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.gray, 50), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
                if (not IS_BULL) and gate_ok
                    n_gate_pass := n_gate_pass + (orbk ? 1 : 0)
                    n_gate_fail := n_gate_fail + (orbk ? 0 : 1)
                    float tp = tp_of(false, pS_lvl)
                    string ofid = f_det_id(tf_time, false)
                    std_total += 1
                    // Same as the bullish side â€” see the note there.
                    bool sent_live = barstate.isrealtime and in_std_enable
                    if in_std_enable
                        alert(build_payload(false, pS_lvl, tp, tf_close, in_std_short_margin, rtag, ofid), alert.freq_all)
                    box  bref = na
                    if in_show_box and not na(pS_boxbar)
                        bref := box.new(pS_boxbar, pS_boxhigh, bar_index, pS_lvl, border_color=color.new(orbk ? color.red : #ef5350, 0), border_width=2, bgcolor=color.new(orbk ? color.red : #ef5350, 80))
                    if in_show_mk
                        label.new(bar_index, tf_high, orbk ? "V" : "v", yloc=yloc.abovebar, style=label.style_label_down, color=color.new(orbk ? color.red : #ef5350, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
                    line enref = na
                    line tpref = na
                    if in_show_tp
                        enref := line.new(bar_index, pS_lvl, bar_index, pS_lvl, color=color.new(#ef5350, 0), width=2)
                        tpref := line.new(bar_index, tp, bar_index, tp, color=color.new(#ef5350, 40), width=1, style=line.style_dashed)
                        label.new(bar_index, tp, "TP " + str.tostring(tp, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(orbk ? color.red : #ef5350, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
                    array.push(of_watch, OrderFlow.new(is_bull=false, is_orbk=orbk, box_top=pS_boxhigh, box_bot=pS_lvl, entry_price=pS_lvl, tp_price=tp, sl_price=na, conf_bar=bar_index, conf_time=tf_time, entered=false, tp_hit=false, armed=false, sl_hit=false, counter_entry=pS_boxhigh, counter_tp=tp_of(true, pS_boxhigh), state="PENDING", fill_bar=na, live_entry=sent_live, b_ref=bref, en_ref=enref, tp_ref=tpref, sl_ref=na, lbl_ref=na, id=ofid))
            pS_lvl := na

// ============================== 9. ORDER FLOW LIFECYCLE + COUNTER ARMING ==============================
if barstate.isconfirmed
    // Trim of_watch. An evicted record stops being managed entirely â€” no TP
    // detection, its counter never arms â€” so what gets dropped matters.
    // Priority, safest first:
    //   1. CLOSED   â€” pure history, nothing left to manage.
    //   2. PENDING  â€” a resting entry that never filled. It has NO path to
    //                 close on its own (every close path requires a fill), so
    //                 stale ones would otherwise occupy a slot forever and
    //                 clog the array. These are the ones that pile up.
    //   3. anything â€” only if neither exists. A live ACTIVE/ARMED position is
    //                 always the very last thing dropped.
    while array.size(of_watch) > MAX_WATCH
        int drop_i = -1
        for k = 0 to array.size(of_watch) - 1
            if array.get(of_watch, k).state == "CLOSED"
                drop_i := k
                break
        if drop_i == -1
            for k = 0 to array.size(of_watch) - 1
                if array.get(of_watch, k).state == "PENDING"
                    drop_i := k
                    break
        if drop_i == -1
            drop_i := 0
        old_of = array.get(of_watch, drop_i)
        if not na(old_of.b_ref)
            box.delete(old_of.b_ref)
        if not na(old_of.en_ref)
            line.delete(old_of.en_ref)
        if not na(old_of.tp_ref)
            line.delete(old_of.tp_ref)
        if not na(old_of.sl_ref)
            line.delete(old_of.sl_ref)
        if not na(old_of.lbl_ref)
            label.delete(old_of.lbl_ref)
        array.remove(of_watch, drop_i)

    // Same rule for counters: an INACTIVE (finished) counter goes before an
    // ARMED/ACTIVE one, so retention can never starve a live counter.
    while array.size(counters) > MAX_CTR
        int drop_c = -1
        for k = 0 to array.size(counters) - 1
            if array.get(counters, k).state == "INACTIVE"
                drop_c := k
                break
        if drop_c == -1
            drop_c := 0
        old_c = array.get(counters, drop_c)
        // Guarded individually â€” the two original-reference lines are optional
        // and are legitimately na while the box and the other lines exist.
        if not na(old_c.b_ref)
            box.delete(old_c.b_ref)
        if not na(old_c.en_ref)
            line.delete(old_c.en_ref)
        if not na(old_c.tp_ref)
            line.delete(old_c.tp_ref)
        if not na(old_c.orig_en_ref)
            line.delete(old_c.orig_en_ref)
        if not na(old_c.orig_tp_ref)
            line.delete(old_c.orig_tp_ref)
        if not na(old_c.lbl_ref)
            label.delete(old_c.lbl_ref)
        array.remove(counters, drop_c)

    // Optional purge of finished counters when retention is OFF. Backward
    // iteration so removals don't skip elements.
    if not in_keep_ctr_done and array.size(counters) > 0
        for j = array.size(counters) - 1 to 0
            cpg = array.get(counters, j)
            if cpg.state == "INACTIVE"
                if not na(cpg.b_ref)
                    box.delete(cpg.b_ref)
                if not na(cpg.en_ref)
                    line.delete(cpg.en_ref)
                if not na(cpg.tp_ref)
                    line.delete(cpg.tp_ref)
                if not na(cpg.orig_en_ref)
                    line.delete(cpg.orig_en_ref)
                if not na(cpg.orig_tp_ref)
                    line.delete(cpg.orig_tp_ref)
                if not na(cpg.lbl_ref)
                    label.delete(cpg.lbl_ref)
                array.remove(counters, j)

    if array.size(of_watch) > 0
        for i = array.size(of_watch) - 1 to 0
            of = array.get(of_watch, i)

            if of.state == "CLOSED"
                // Drawings are dropped when the record is being purged OR when
                // completed flows are set to hidden. Deleting BEFORE removing
                // the record matters â€” otherwise the box/lines/label are
                // orphaned on the chart forever (the exact bug class hunted
                // down earlier in the Counter Entry script's eviction path).
                bool purge_rec  = not in_keep_std_done
                bool drop_draws = purge_rec or not in_show_std_done
                if drop_draws
                    if not na(of.b_ref)
                        box.delete(of.b_ref)
                        of.b_ref := na
                    if not na(of.en_ref)
                        line.delete(of.en_ref)
                        of.en_ref := na
                    if not na(of.tp_ref)
                        line.delete(of.tp_ref)
                        of.tp_ref := na
                    if not na(of.sl_ref)
                        line.delete(of.sl_ref)
                        of.sl_ref := na
                    if not na(of.lbl_ref)
                        label.delete(of.lbl_ref)
                        of.lbl_ref := na
                if purge_rec
                    array.remove(of_watch, i)
                else
                    array.set(of_watch, i, of)
                continue

            if bar_index <= of.conf_bar
                continue

            // fill check
            if not of.entered
                bool touch = of.is_bull ? (tf_low <= of.entry_price) : (tf_high >= of.entry_price)
                if touch
                    of.entered := true
                    of.state := "ACTIVE"
                    of.fill_bar := bar_index

            // TP check â€” only on bars AFTER the fill bar. Chronology: the entry
            // alert only goes out at the close of the bar where the fill is
            // detected, so the position does not exist on the exchange until
            // that bar has closed. A TP "touch" during the fill bar itself is
            // therefore not reachable in reality and must be ignored â€” a trade
            // has to go PENDING -> ACTIVE -> (next bar or later) TP.
            // Runs regardless of armed state, so a late recovery to the STD's
            // own TP is never missed once a counter has armed/filled.
            if of.entered and bar_index > of.fill_bar and not of.tp_hit and not of.sl_hit
                bool tp_touch = of.is_bull ? (tf_high >= of.tp_price) : (tf_low <= of.tp_price)
                if tp_touch
                    of.tp_hit := true
                    of.state := "CLOSED"
                    std_completed += 1
                    // Freeze the drawn levels at the closing bar. This path
                    // short-circuits with `continue`, so without this the
                    // lines would stop one bar short of where they resolved.
                    if not na(of.en_ref)
                        line.set_x2(of.en_ref, bar_index)
                    if not na(of.tp_ref)
                        line.set_x2(of.tp_ref, bar_index)
                    if not na(of.sl_ref)
                        line.set_x2(of.sl_ref, bar_index)
                    // The ORIGINAL reached its own TP. If a counter had already
                    // filled, a reduce-only SL limit is still resting on the book
                    // for this position â€” cancel it, or it is left orphaned once
                    // the position closes on its own TP.
                    if of.armed and array.size(counters) > 0
                        for j = array.size(counters) - 1 to 0
                            c = array.get(counters, j)
                            if c.of_id == of.id and (c.state == "ARMED" or c.state == "ACTIVE")
                                // The counter is NOT touched here. It keeps its
                                // own lifecycle â€” armed -> filled -> its own TP â€”
                                // independent of whatever the original does. Its
                                // entry limit is live on Bybit, so marking it
                                // finished would desync Pine from a real order,
                                // and counting it would inflate "Done" with a
                                // counter that may never have opened.
                                // Only the SL on the ORIGINAL is now orphaned.
                                // It exists only if the counter already filled.
                                // c.bot_linked: a CHART ONLY counter never sent
                                // anything, so there is no SL on the exchange
                                // to cancel and firing this would reference an
                                // id the bot cannot resolve.
                                if c.state == "ACTIVE" and c.bot_linked
                                    // If this same bar also reached the counter's
                                    // TP, the SL fired with it â€” nothing left to
                                    // cancel. Intrabar order is unknowable, so
                                    // assume it fired.
                                    bool ctr_tp_same_bar = c.is_long ? (tf_high >= c.tp_price) : (tf_low <= c.tp_price)
                                    if not ctr_tp_same_bar
                                        alert(build_cancel_sl_payload(of.id, tf_close), alert.freq_all)
                                break
                    array.set(of_watch, i, of)
                    continue

            // continuous far-end-cleared check -> arm counter (pre-arm only)
            // Arming IS the counter's confirmation, so the same validity rule
            // applies: a neutral / inside candle can never arm one, no matter
            // where its body closed. Only the arming is gated â€” the counter's
            // own fill, its TP and the SL it sets on the original all execute
            // on any candle.
            if of.entered and not of.tp_hit and not of.armed and not of.sl_hit and not neutral
                float body_top = math.max(tf_open, tf_close)
                float body_bot = math.min(tf_open, tf_close)
                bool far_end_cleared = of.is_bull ? (body_bot <= of.box_bot) : (body_top >= of.box_top)
                if far_end_cleared
                    // No array-size gate here on purpose. Refusing to arm
                    // because the array happens to be full would silently
                    // close a live order flow for an internal housekeeping
                    // reason â€” the trim at the top of this section handles
                    // capacity, and it evicts finished records first.
                    if in_counter_enable
                        of.armed := true
                        of.state := "ARMED"
                        counter_total += 1
                        // âš  THE REPLAYED-ORIGINAL TRAP. Pine rebuilds this
                        // whole array from history every time the script is
                        // loaded or an input changes, and historical bars fire
                        // NO alerts. A flow that never reached its TP stays
                        // ACTIVE and is the LAST thing the trim evicts, so a
                        // replayed flow can survive for months and then have
                        // its far end swept on a REALTIME bar. The arm alert
                        // would then go out carrying an id the bot has never
                        // seen: it opens the counter, fails to resolve the
                        // original, and leaves that counter running with no
                        // hedge and no stop. This happened live on 8003 on
                        // 2026-08-19 â€” counter armed from a 2026-05-22 flow.
                        // The counter is still tracked and drawn (the chart
                        // stays useful for study) but marked CHART ONLY and
                        // NOTHING is sent.
                        bool ctr_linked = of.live_entry
                        array.push(counters, CounterRecord.new(is_long=not of.is_bull, entry_price=of.counter_entry, tp_price=of.counter_tp, box_top=of.box_top, box_bot=of.box_bot, entry_time=tf_time, conf_time=of.conf_time, conf_bar=bar_index, state="ARMED", end_time=na, fill_bar=na, bot_linked=ctr_linked, b_ref=na, en_ref=na, tp_ref=na, orig_en_ref=na, orig_tp_ref=na, lbl_ref=na, of_id=of.id))
                        // ARM = CONFIRMED. The alert goes out at this candle's
                        // close and the entry limit rests on Bybit from here.
                        // Nothing is held inside the indicator waiting for a
                        // touch â€” the exchange fills it at the exact level.
                        // The counter is the opposite side of the original, but
                        // its margin is looked up by the ORIGINAL's direction â€”
                        // that is what keeps the size ratio to the position it
                        // actually hedges.
                        if ctr_linked
                            bool   ctr_is_long = not of.is_bull
                            float  ctr_margin  = of.is_bull ? in_ctr_for_long_margin : in_ctr_for_short_margin
                            alert(build_counter_arm_payload(ctr_is_long, of.counter_entry, tf_close, ctr_margin, of.id, of.counter_tp), alert.freq_all)
                    else
                        // Counter Trade genuinely switched off by the user â€”
                        // the flow rides with no SL and is done here.
                        of.state := "CLOSED"
                        std_completed += 1
                        array.set(of_watch, i, of)
                        continue

            // NOTE: the counter's own fill/TP transitions used to live HERE,
            // nested inside this loop and gated on `of.armed`. That was a bug.
            // The moment the original closed it was removed from of_watch (or
            // short-circuited past this point when retention kept it), and the
            // only code that advanced its counter went with it â€” the counter
            // froze in ACTIVE forever, box stretching to the right edge, no
            // matter how many times price crossed its TP. Live charts showed
            // 129 of 357 counters stuck this way.
            // The counter now runs its own loop in section 9b, which reaches
            // back to the original only when it needs to touch it. See there.

            // extend STD visuals
            if not na(of.en_ref)
                line.set_x2(of.en_ref, bar_index)
            if not na(of.tp_ref)
                line.set_x2(of.tp_ref, bar_index)
            if not na(of.sl_ref)
                line.set_x2(of.sl_ref, bar_index)

            // STD info label â€” created once on the first bar the flow is
            // FILLED, then follows the right edge with live state. Only filled
            // flows get one: a pending flow is just a resting limit order and
            // its box/lines already say everything, so labelling every pending
            // flow would bury the chart on a busy timeframe.
            if in_show_std_lbl and of.entered
                string of_state = of.armed ? (na(of.sl_price) ? "Armed" : "Active + SL") : "Active"
                float  of_delta = ((of.tp_price / of.entry_price) - 1) * 100
                string of_lbl   = "[" + tf_actual + "] STD " + (of.is_bull ? "â–² LONG" : "â–¼ SHORT") + " [" + of_state + "]" +
                       "\nEntry: " + str.tostring(of.entry_price, "#.#####") +
                       "\nTP: "    + str.tostring(of.tp_price, "#.#####") + "  (" + str.tostring(of_delta, "#.##") + "%)" +
                       (na(of.sl_price) ? "" : "\nSL: " + str.tostring(of.sl_price, "#.#####")) +
                       "\nid: " + of.id
                color of_lbl_col = of.is_bull ? color.new(#26a69a, 20) : color.new(#ef5350, 20)
                if na(of.lbl_ref)
                    of.lbl_ref := label.new(bar_index, of.entry_price, text=of_lbl, style=label.style_label_left, color=of_lbl_col, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
                else
                    label.set_x(of.lbl_ref, bar_index)
                    label.set_y(of.lbl_ref, of.entry_price)
                    label.set_text(of.lbl_ref, of_lbl)
                    label.set_color(of.lbl_ref, of_lbl_col)
            else if not na(of.lbl_ref)
                label.delete(of.lbl_ref)
                of.lbl_ref := na

            array.set(of_watch, i, of)

// ============================== 9b. COUNTER LIFECYCLE (INDEPENDENT) ==========
// The counter's own state machine, deliberately NOT nested inside the order
// flow loop. A counter's entry limit and its TP are real live orders resting on
// Bybit, so they must keep advancing whatever happens to the original â€”
// including the original closing on its own TP and being evicted from of_watch
// entirely. Nesting this was the bug that froze 129 of 357 counters in ACTIVE.
//
// Nothing here fires an alert. The counter's TP and the original's SL have both
// been resting on the exchange since the counter's entry filled, so the real
// closes happen there. This only keeps the chart and the table honest.
//
// The original is looked up by id ONLY on a transition bar (a fill or a TP), so
// the nested scan costs nothing on ordinary bars. If the original is already
// gone, the counter simply carries on alone.
if barstate.isconfirmed and array.size(counters) > 0
    for j = 0 to array.size(counters) - 1
        c = array.get(counters, j)
        if c.state == "INACTIVE"
            continue

        // ---- counter's entry fills ----
        if c.state == "ARMED" and bar_index > c.conf_bar
            bool ctr_touch = c.is_long ? (tf_low <= c.entry_price) : (tf_high >= c.entry_price)
            if ctr_touch
                c.state    := "ACTIVE"
                c.fill_bar := bar_index
                // Mirror the dynamic SL onto the original, if it is still tracked.
                if array.size(of_watch) > 0
                    for k = 0 to array.size(of_watch) - 1
                        ofsl = array.get(of_watch, k)
                        if ofsl.id == c.of_id and ofsl.state != "CLOSED"
                            ofsl.sl_price := c.tp_price
                            if in_show_tp
                                ofsl.sl_ref := line.new(bar_index, c.tp_price, bar_index, c.tp_price, color=color.new(color.orange, 0), width=1, style=line.style_dotted)
                            array.set(of_watch, k, ofsl)
                            break

        // ---- counter reaches its own TP ----
        if c.state == "ACTIVE" and bar_index > c.fill_bar
            bool ctr_tp = c.is_long ? (tf_high >= c.tp_price) : (tf_low <= c.tp_price)
            if ctr_tp
                c.state    := "INACTIVE"
                c.end_time := tf_time
                counter_completed += 1
                // The original is stopped out at this same level â€” but only if
                // it is still open. It may already have closed on its own TP
                // earlier this same bar, in which case section 9 already counted
                // it and touching it again would double-count std_completed.
                if array.size(of_watch) > 0
                    for k = 0 to array.size(of_watch) - 1
                        ofcl = array.get(of_watch, k)
                        if ofcl.id == c.of_id
                            if ofcl.state != "CLOSED" and not ofcl.tp_hit and not ofcl.sl_hit
                                ofcl.sl_hit := true
                                ofcl.state  := "CLOSED"
                                std_completed += 1
                                array.set(of_watch, k, ofcl)
                            break

        array.set(counters, j, c)

// ============================== 10. COUNTER VISUALIZATION ==============================
if barstate.isconfirmed and array.size(counters) > 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(counters) - 1
        c = array.get(counters, i)
        bool hide_this = (c.state == "INACTIVE" and not in_show_counter_done) or not in_show_counter or (not c.bot_linked and not in_show_ctr_unlinked)
        if hide_this
            if not na(c.b_ref)
                box.delete(c.b_ref)
                c.b_ref := na
            // Individually guarded: the two original-reference lines are
            // optional now, so they can legitimately be na while the rest exist.
            if not na(c.en_ref)
                line.delete(c.en_ref)
                c.en_ref := na
            if not na(c.tp_ref)
                line.delete(c.tp_ref)
                c.tp_ref := na
            if not na(c.orig_en_ref)
                line.delete(c.orig_en_ref)
                c.orig_en_ref := na
            if not na(c.orig_tp_ref)
                line.delete(c.orig_tp_ref)
                c.orig_tp_ref := na
            if not na(c.lbl_ref)
                label.delete(c.lbl_ref)
                c.lbl_ref := na
            array.set(counters, i, c)
            continue

        color brd_c = c.state == "ACTIVE" ? (c.is_long ? color.new(#00e676,0) : color.new(#ff1744,0)) :
                      c.state == "ARMED"  ? color.new(color.orange, 40) :
                      color.new(color.gray, 50)
        color bg_c  = c.state == "ACTIVE" ? (c.is_long ? color.new(color.green,85) : color.new(color.red,85)) :
                      c.state == "ARMED"  ? (c.is_long ? color.new(color.green,92) : color.new(color.red,92)) :
                      color.new(color.gray, 92)
        int brd_w = c.state == "ACTIVE" ? 3 : 1
        // A CHART ONLY counter is drawn deliberately dull and thin so it can
        // never be mistaken at a glance for a live hedged position.
        if not c.bot_linked
            brd_c := color.new(color.gray, 30)
            bg_c  := color.new(color.gray, 95)
            brd_w := 1
        int right_e = c.state == "INACTIVE" ? (not na(c.end_time) ? c.end_time : time) : time

        // Original signal's entry and TP on the opposite side of the box
        float orig_entry     = c.is_long ? c.box_bot : c.box_top
        float orig_tp_price  = tp_of(not c.is_long, orig_entry)
        color orig_e_col     = c.is_long ? color.new(#00e676, 65) : color.new(#ff1744, 65)
        color orig_tp_col    = color.new(color.gray, 40)

        string state_txt = c.state == "ACTIVE" ? "Active" : c.state == "ARMED" ? "Armed" : "Completed"
        float  delta_pct = ((c.tp_price / c.entry_price) - 1) * 100
        string lbl_txt = "[" + tf_actual + "] âš¡ Counter " + (c.is_long ? "â–² LONG" : "â–¼ SHORT") + " [" + state_txt + "]" +
               (c.bot_linked ? "" : "\nâš  CHART ONLY â€” original was never sent") +
               "\nEntry: " + str.tostring(c.entry_price, "#.#####") +
               "\nTP: "    + str.tostring(c.tp_price, "#.#####") + "  (" + str.tostring(delta_pct, "#.##") + "%)" +
               (c.bot_linked ? "\nSL on original: " + str.tostring(c.tp_price, "#.#####") : "") +
               "\nid: " + c.of_id
        float box_h = c.box_top - c.box_bot
        float lbl_y = c.is_long ? (c.box_bot - box_h * 0.5) : (c.box_top + box_h * 0.5)

        // Entry line colour follows the same dulling rule as the box.
        color ctr_en_col = c.bot_linked ? (c.is_long ? color.new(#00e676,20) : color.new(#ff1744,20)) : color.new(color.gray, 30)
        color ctr_tp_col = c.bot_linked ? color.new(color.orange, 40) : color.new(color.gray, 55)

        if na(c.b_ref)
            c.b_ref       := box.new(c.entry_time, c.box_top, right_e, c.box_bot, brd_c, brd_w, line.style_solid, xloc=xloc.bar_time, bgcolor=bg_c)
            c.en_ref      := line.new(c.entry_time, c.entry_price, right_e, c.entry_price, color=ctr_en_col, width=3, style=line.style_solid, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
            c.tp_ref      := line.new(c.entry_time, c.tp_price, right_e, c.tp_price, color=ctr_tp_col, width=1, style=line.style_dashed, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
            // The original's levels are OPTIONAL â€” they double this counter's
            // line cost and the 500-line budget is the binding constraint. See
            // the MAX_CTR note in section 4.
            if in_show_ctr_orig_lines
                c.orig_en_ref := line.new(c.entry_time, orig_entry, right_e, orig_entry, color=orig_e_col, width=2, style=line.style_dashed, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
                c.orig_tp_ref := line.new(c.entry_time, orig_tp_price, right_e, orig_tp_price, color=orig_tp_col, width=1, style=line.style_dashed, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
            c.lbl_ref     := label.new(right_e, lbl_y, text=lbl_txt, style=c.is_long ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=brd_c, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        else
            box.set_right(c.b_ref, right_e)
            box.set_border_color(c.b_ref, brd_c)
            box.set_border_width(c.b_ref, brd_w)
            box.set_bgcolor(c.b_ref, bg_c)
            line.set_x2(c.en_ref, right_e)
            line.set_color(c.en_ref, ctr_en_col)
            line.set_x2(c.tp_ref, right_e)
            line.set_color(c.tp_ref, ctr_tp_col)
            // Toggled on after the counter was drawn: create them now.
            if in_show_ctr_orig_lines and na(c.orig_en_ref)
                c.orig_en_ref := line.new(c.entry_time, orig_entry, right_e, orig_entry, color=orig_e_col, width=2, style=line.style_dashed, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
                c.orig_tp_ref := line.new(c.entry_time, orig_tp_price, right_e, orig_tp_price, color=orig_tp_col, width=1, style=line.style_dashed, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
            // Toggled off: reclaim the two lines immediately.
            if not in_show_ctr_orig_lines and not na(c.orig_en_ref)
                line.delete(c.orig_en_ref)
                line.delete(c.orig_tp_ref)
                c.orig_en_ref := na
                c.orig_tp_ref := na
            if not na(c.orig_en_ref)
                line.set_x2(c.orig_en_ref, right_e)
            if not na(c.orig_tp_ref)
                line.set_x2(c.orig_tp_ref, right_e)
            label.set_x(c.lbl_ref, right_e)
            label.set_y(c.lbl_ref, lbl_y)
            label.set_text(c.lbl_ref, lbl_txt)
            label.set_color(c.lbl_ref, brd_c)

        array.set(counters, i, c)

// ============================== 10b. LIVE MARKERS AT RIGHT EDGE ==============
// On the last bar only, print a compact price tag just past the current candle
// for every level that is still live, so the numbers can be read at a glance
// without hovering over the lines. Pine rolls back last-bar drawings on every
// tick, so these refresh in place instead of accumulating.
if barstate.islast and in_show_live
    int lm_off = 6

    // --- live STD order flows (filled and not yet closed) ---
    if array.size(of_watch) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(of_watch) - 1
            ofl = array.get(of_watch, i)
            if ofl.entered and ofl.state != "CLOSED"
                color lm_c = ofl.is_bull ? color.new(#26a69a, 10) : color.new(#ef5350, 10)
                label.new(bar_index + lm_off, ofl.entry_price, text=(ofl.is_bull ? "â–² " : "â–¼ ") + str.tostring(ofl.entry_price, "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=lm_c, textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
                label.new(bar_index + lm_off, ofl.tp_price, text="TP " + str.tostring(ofl.tp_price, "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(color.teal, 55), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
                if not na(ofl.sl_price)
                    label.new(bar_index + lm_off, ofl.sl_price, text="SL " + str.tostring(ofl.sl_price, "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(color.orange, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)

    // --- live counters (entry filled, TP not reached yet) ---
    if array.size(counters) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(counters) - 1
            cl = array.get(counters, i)
            // CHART ONLY counters are excluded: a price tag at the right edge
            // reads as a live position, and this one does not exist anywhere.
            if cl.state == "ACTIVE" and cl.bot_linked
                color lm_cc = cl.is_long ? color.new(#00e676, 10) : color.new(#ff1744, 10)
                label.new(bar_index + lm_off, cl.entry_price, text="âš¡ " + (cl.is_long ? "â–² " : "â–¼ ") + str.tostring(cl.entry_price, "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=lm_cc, textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
                label.new(bar_index + lm_off, cl.tp_price, text="âš¡ TP " + str.tostring(cl.tp_price, "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(color.orange, 40), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)

// ============================== 11. STRUCTURE UPDATE ==============================
if not neutral
    if bull_v
        last_valid_high := tf_high
        last_valid_low  := tf_low
        lgv_bar := bar_index
        lgv_high := tf_high
        lgv_low  := tf_low
    if bear_v
        last_valid_high := tf_high
        last_valid_low  := tf_low
        lbv_bar := bar_index
        lbv_high := tf_high
        lbv_low  := tf_low

// ============================== 12. STATS TABLE ==============================
if barstate.islast and in_show_table
    int std_pending = 0
    int std_active  = 0
    if array.size(of_watch) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(of_watch) - 1
            ofw = array.get(of_watch, i)
            if ofw.state == "PENDING"
                std_pending += 1
            else if ofw.state == "ACTIVE" or ofw.state == "ARMED"
                std_active += 1

    int ctr_pending = 0
    int ctr_active  = 0
    int ctr_done    = 0
    int ctr_ghost   = 0
    if array.size(counters) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(counters) - 1
            cw = array.get(counters, i)
            if cw.state == "ARMED"
                ctr_pending += 1
            else if cw.state == "ACTIVE"
                ctr_active += 1
            else if cw.state == "INACTIVE"
                ctr_done += 1
            // Tracked and drawn, but nothing was ever sent for them because
            // their order flow only ever existed in Pine's history replay.
            if not cw.bot_linked
                ctr_ghost += 1

    table.delete(stat_tbl)
    stat_tbl := table.new(get_table_pos(in_tbl_pos), 5, 5, border_width=1)
    color hb = color.new(#37474f, 20)
    color lb = color.new(#455a64, 80)
    color wt = color.new(color.white, 0)
    color okc = color.new(#66bb6a, 0)
    color pdc = color.new(#ffb74d, 0)
    color dnc = color.new(#42a5f5, 0)

    table.cell(stat_tbl, 0, 0, (GATED ? "STD-ORBK " : "STD-PLAIN ") + (IS_BULL ? "â–²" : "â–¼"), bgcolor=hb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 1, 0, "Total", bgcolor=hb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 2, 0, "Pend", bgcolor=hb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 3, 0, "Active", bgcolor=hb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 4, 0, "Done", bgcolor=hb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(stat_tbl, 0, 1, "STD OF", bgcolor=lb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 1, 1, str.tostring(std_total), bgcolor=lb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 2, 1, str.tostring(std_pending), bgcolor=lb, text_color=pdc, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 3, 1, str.tostring(std_active), bgcolor=lb, text_color=okc, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 4, 1, str.tostring(std_completed), bgcolor=lb, text_color=dnc, text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(stat_tbl, 0, 2, "Counter", bgcolor=lb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 1, 2, str.tostring(counter_total), bgcolor=lb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 2, 2, str.tostring(ctr_pending), bgcolor=lb, text_color=pdc, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 3, 2, str.tostring(ctr_active), bgcolor=lb, text_color=okc, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 4, 2, str.tostring(counter_completed), bgcolor=lb, text_color=dnc, text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(stat_tbl, 0, 3, "Toggles", bgcolor=hb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 1, 3, "STD:" + (in_std_enable ? "ON" : "OFF"), bgcolor=hb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 2, 3, "CTR:" + (in_counter_enable ? "ON" : "OFF"), bgcolor=hb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 3, 3, "Lev:" + str.tostring(in_lev, "#"), bgcolor=hb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 4, 3, tf_actual, bgcolor=hb, text_color=wt, text_size=size.tiny)

    table.cell(stat_tbl, 0, 4, "ORBK y/n", bgcolor=lb, text_color=color.new(color.white,20), text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 1, 4, str.tostring(n_gate_pass), bgcolor=lb, text_color=okc, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 2, 4, str.tostring(n_gate_fail), bgcolor=lb, text_color=pdc, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 3, 4, "Chart only", bgcolor=lb, text_color=color.new(color.white,20), text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(stat_tbl, 4, 4, str.tostring(ctr_ghost), bgcolor=lb, text_color=(ctr_ghost > 0 ? color.new(color.gray, 0) : wt), text_size=size.tiny)